---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Seat Selection Practice: Budgets, Aisles & Backups | StageDrill';
const description =
  'Learn practical strategies for spotting connected concert seats, avoiding center-aisle split traps, setting virtual budgets, and pivoting under time pressure.';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/guides/seat-selection-practice/"
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-4 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-500">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-slate-900">Home</a>
      <span class="mx-1.5">/</span>
      <span class="text-slate-900">Seat Selection Strategy</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="display-h1 text-slate-950">
      Seat Selection Practice: How to Master Budgets, Adjacent Seats &amp; Backup Zones
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
      Most wasted seconds on an interactive seat map happen when shoppers recalculate totals on the fly or click seats that look neighboring until you notice a walkway aisle in between. A structured pre-sale mental checklist eliminates hesitation.
    </p>

    <section class="mt-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="section-h2 text-slate-950">1. Why Seat 4 and Seat 5 Are Often Not Adjacent</h2>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700 sm:text-base">
        Numbered seats frequently run consecutively across a walkway aisle. Even though Seat 4 and Seat 5 differ by 1, a physical aisle sits between them. In StageDrill, every row splits into a left block (Seats 1–4) and a right block (Seats 5–8) separated by a clearly marked <strong>AISLE</strong> corridor:
      </p>

      <figure class="mt-4">
        <img
          src="/images/aisle-adjacency-diagram.svg"
          alt="Adjacency diagram illustrating Seats 1 to 4 on the left block separated by the center aisle from Seats 5 to 8 on the right block"
          width="880"
          height="320"
          fetchpriority="high"
          decoding="async"
          class="h-auto w-full rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 shadow-sm"
        />
        <figcaption class="mt-2 text-xs text-slate-600">
          Valid contiguous blocks stay inside S1&ndash;S4 or S5&ndash;S8; pairing Seat 4 with Seat 5 fails the aisle check.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-center text-xs font-bold text-slate-200">
        <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-lg items-center justify-center gap-1.5">
          <span class="rounded bg-sky-900 px-2.5 py-2">S1</span>
          <span class="rounded bg-sky-900 px-2.5 py-2">S2</span>
          <span class="rounded bg-sky-900 px-2.5 py-2">S3</span>
          <span class="rounded border border-amber-400 bg-sky-900 px-2.5 py-2">S4</span>
          <span class="mx-2 rounded border border-dashed border-slate-500 px-2.5 py-2 text-slate-400">AISLE</span>
          <span class="rounded border border-amber-400 bg-sky-900 px-2.5 py-2">S5</span>
          <span class="rounded bg-sky-900 px-2.5 py-2">S6</span>
          <span class="rounded bg-sky-900 px-2.5 py-2">S7</span>
          <span class="rounded bg-sky-900 px-2.5 py-2">S8</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-xs font-normal text-slate-400">
          Valid 4-seat runs: S1–S4 or S5–S8. Selecting S3–S6 crosses the walkway and fails adjacency.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8 space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700 sm:text-base">
      <h2 class="section-h2 text-slate-950">2. Lock Your All-In Per-Ticket Cap First</h2>
      <p>
        Before an arena map opens, convert your group total into a firm per-ticket maximum (for example, $560 for 4 tickets = $140/seat). On StageDrill, seats priced above your per-ticket limit display a dashed amber outline and <code>$!</code> badge so you can train your eye to skip unaffordable tiers immediately.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8 space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700 sm:text-base">
      <h2 class="section-h2 text-slate-950">3. Carry One Primary Zone and Two Backup Zones</h2>
      <p>
        When primary floor or lower-bowl rows sell through mid-selection, deciding where to look next eats 10–15 seconds. Always name a lower-cost backup section before clicking. In our <strong>Live Scramble</strong> mode, Wave 1 tightens your preferred section while keeping a guaranteed backup block open so you can practice zero-hesitation pivots.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-extrabold text-slate-950">Put Strategy Into Practice</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a
          href="/practice/?mode=quick&difficulty=hard&seed=arena-101"
          class="rounded-xl bg-indigo-600 px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-white hover:bg-indigo-500"
        >
          Try Hard Quick Pick →
        </a>
        <a
          href="/guides/ticketmaster-training/"
          class="rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-slate-50 px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 hover:bg-slate-100"
        >
          Read Training Scope Guide
        </a>
        <a
          href="/guides/concert-seat-selection-basics/"
          class="rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-slate-50 px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 hover:bg-slate-100"
        >
          Seat Selection Basics
        </a>
        <a
          href="/guides/scoring-explained/"
          class="rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-slate-50 px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 hover:bg-slate-100"
        >
          Scoring Explained
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
